    "result_text": "The full test suite (a single `AcceptanceTest` class) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist rejection for owner emails.\n\n**Where the logic went** \u2014 `EmailNormalizer` (`rest/validation/EmailNormalizer.java`) already owns email normalization and syntactic validation, so the disposable-domain policy is a cohesive addition there rather than a new catch-all:\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n- Added `isDisposable(String email)` \u2014 extracts the domain after the last `@`, lower-cases it, and checks membership. Null/malformed input returns `false` (those cases are already handled by `isValid`).\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 in `OwnerRestControllerV1`, both `addOwner` and `updateOwner` now reject with `400 BAD_REQUEST` when a supplied email is invalid **or** disposable, folded into the existing email-validation guard so an absent email is still allowed.\n\nThe new acceptance test (`x@mailinator.com` \u2192 400) passes and nothing else regressed.",
